{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01FHqyfHDXvDYLDZGng9HbiW", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illinois\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ebsco.com/research-starters/history/illinois-admitted-union\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/US-IL\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/when-was-the-us-state-of-illinois-founded.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rarenewspapers.com/newspaper/701327\"}, {\"url\": \"https://repwindhorst.com/?p=4918\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.myheritage.com/wiki/Illinois\"}, {\"url\": \"https://repschmidt.com/?p=2222\"}, {\"url\": \"https://repkeicher.com/?p=4198\"}, {\"url\": \"https://repkeicher.com/?p=4958\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:59:27.862Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Illinois admitted to the Union December 3, 1818 statehood", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_018CvEnbmzPcF25BexsPpTfJ", "content": [{"title": "Illinois", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illinois"}, {"title": "Illinois Admitted to the Union", "url": "https://ebsco.com/research-starters/history/illinois-admitted-union"}, {"title": "US IL", "url": "https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/US-IL"}, {"title": "When Did Illinois Become a State?", "url": "https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/when-was-the-us-state-of-illinois-founded.html"}, {"title": "www.rarenewspapers.com", "url": "https://www.rarenewspapers.com/newspaper/701327"}, {"title": "Rep. Windhorst Marks Illinois Statehood Day", "url": "https://repwindhorst.com/?p=4918"}, {"title": "www.myheritage.com", "url": "https://www.myheritage.com/wiki/Illinois"}, {"title": "repschmidt.com", "url": "https://repschmidt.com/?p=2222"}, {"title": "Illinois’ Journey to Statehood", "url": "https://repkeicher.com/?p=4198"}, {"title": "Celebrating Illinois’ Statehood on December 3", "url": "https://repkeicher.com/?p=4958"}]}, "The search confirms that Illinois was admitted to the Union on December 3, 1818, as the 21st state. Sources agree on the date, though they differ on the population at the time.\n\n- **Date and rank:** Multiple sources, including a Wikipedia infobox, list the admission date and the 21st-state rank. President James Monroe signed the resolution admitting Illinois as the 21st state.\n- **Population hurdle:** The Northwest Ordinance set a population requirement that Illinois struggled to meet. One source puts the requirement at 60,000 free inhabitants, while the state had roughly 40,000 residents. Another source gives the population as approximately 35,000, so the reported figures vary.\n- **Route to statehood:** According to EBSCO, territories with populations over 35,000 could still petition for statehood under certain conditions, which led the territorial legislature to apply for admission.\n- **Territorial background:** Illinois became part of the Northwest Territory, and the Congress established the Illinois Territory on February 3, 1809. A constitutional convention followed in Kaskaskia in 1818.\n\nSources: Wikipedia (Illinois), EBSCO Research Starters, Rep. Windhorst's Statehood Day page, and the Kaskaskia convention details from repkeicher.com."], "durationSeconds": 5.476901624999998, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01FHqyfHDXvDYLDZGng9HbiW", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgDXh1S3VErDPRy65mMyg", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**答案：1818 年 12 月 3 日。** 这艘消防船叫 *Illinois*，伊利诺伊州在这一天作为美国第 21 个州加入联邦。\n\n- 1908 年，伯灵顿铁路码头的一座粮仓起火，墙倒下来把 *Illinois* 号砸沉在芝加哥河里，水深约 20 英尺。后来船被打捞起来，又回去服役了。两份 1908 年 8 月的报纸写了沉船经过，打捞的事只在维基百科上看到。两个维基页面写的船的投入使用年份不一样（1888 和 1899），不过这不影响答案。\n- 伊利诺伊州在 1818 年 12 月 3 日成为第 21 个州。在这之前，1809 年 2 月 3 日已经设了伊利诺伊领地。如果题目说的“founded”是指成立领地，答案就是 1809 年；一般理解是成为州，就是 1818 年。\n\n共搜了 2 次。\n\n依据的网址：\n- [Illinois (fireboat) – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illinois_(fireboat))\n- [Fireboats of Chicago – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireboats_of_Chicago)\n- [Valentine Democrat, 1908-08-13](https://nebnewspapers.unl.edu/lccn/sn95069780/1908-08-13/ed-1/seq-7/ocr)\n- [Nebraska newspaper, 1908-08-06](https://nebnewspapers.unl.edu/lccn/2010270500/1908-08-06/ed-1/seq-8.pdf)\n- [Illinois – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illinois)\n- [Illinois Admitted to the Union – EBSCO](https://ebsco.com/research-starters/history/illinois-admitted-union)\n- [When Did Illinois Become a State? – WorldAtlas](https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/when-was-the-us-state-of-illinois-founded.html)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1088, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5690, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1088}, "output_tokens": 727, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:59:40.313Z", "request_id": "req_011CgDXgzymHu7T6SpwnxRJf"}
